Fix round 1. The task reviewer found 2 Important issues in your Task 10 commit (f97bf8f). Fix both, re-run covering tests, commit, push, append fix report to task-10-report.md. Also your report's phrase "sdc_evolve 种子回灌 → 完整跑通" overstated reality (sdc_evolve early-exited on the legacy all-zero results.json; no seed was ever written) — correct that in the appended fix report (诚实红线).

Open findings:

1. **Back-fill (回灌) is functionally dead for new-framework hits.** feedback_loop.sh delegates to legacy sdc_evolve.sh which reads output/distributed/results.json (all boards sdc_hits=0) — it can never see the new framework's hits, and in your synthetic test it provably early-exited with no seed written. Fix: feedback.py already resolves hash→pb→instructions — implement direct back-fill in feedback.py: `reseed(hits, pb_dir, seeds_dir="seeds/evolved")` that writes the hit snapshot's instruction bytes to seeds/evolved/<hash>.bin (or copies the .pb with a manifest mapping hash→file if raw insn extraction is lossy — choose what preserves replayability; document choice). feedback_loop.sh calls this instead of (or before) the legacy best-effort call. Keep the legacy call if you want, but the primary path must be the direct one.

2. **replay-confirm red line not enforced by the pipeline.** replay_confirm() exists but nothing calls it; given a real hit, the loop amplifies without confirmation. Fix the loop flow: hits → for each hit, resolve to a replayable per-snapshot corpus (implement the generate_corpus packaging step: snap_tool make already gave .pb; run snap_tool --target_platform=arm-neoverse-n1 generate_corpus <pb> --out=<corpus> per hit — same verified pipeline as exp03/exp05) → replay_confirm(corpus_file, n=3) → only confirmed (reproduced==n) hits go to reseed(); transient/partial → marked transient in hits.json and excluded from reseed (quarantine semantics). E5-style hash-less group hits: label action "quarantine" not "replay-confirm" (minor finding, fix together).

Covering verification (all with real output pasted):
(a) test_feedback.py ALL PASS (extend tests for reseed + the loop gating: synthetic hit that is NOT reproducible must NOT be reseeded; you can simulate by pointing replay at a healthy snapshot corpus whose "hit" is synthetic — the replay returns no failure → transient → no reseed; and a reseed unit test with a temp seeds_dir);
(b) synthetic-hit end-to-end rerun of feedback_loop.sh: show the NEW flow — hit branch → generate_corpus packaging → replay 3x → (with your synthetic setup it will honestly be NOT_REPRODUCED/transient) → NO seed written, exit code and output reflecting the honest gate. Then also demonstrate the confirmed path once: point the synthetic hit at a corpus package and mock/force replay_confirm to return confirmed OR construct a genuinely-failing snapshot if feasible cheaply — if forcing is the only option, do it via a unit test on the gating function (test the gate, not the fabricate) and say so plainly;
(c) idle-spin rerun on E3 → 无命中 output unchanged;
(d) regression test_device_pool.py ALL PASS.

Commit message: "fix(experiment): 反馈闭环实化——直接回灌替代legacy死路+replay-confirm三复跑gate强制+quarantine语义". Push. Return short contract: status, commit sha, one-line test summary, concerns.

